  "term": "xeroderma pigmentosum",
  "definition": "Xeroderma pigmentosum is an inherited disorder in which the body cannot properly repair ultraviolet-related DNA damage. It causes extreme sensitivity to sunlight, early skin changes such as freckle-like spots and lesions, and a high risk of skin cancers, sometimes along with eye and nervous system problems.",
